What is a Pipeline?

A pipeline is a series of steps arranged in order to complete a task.

Simple real-life example: Making tea ☕
Water
  ↓
Boil Water
  ↓
Add Tea Powder
  ↓
Add Milk & Sugar
  ↓
Filter
  ↓
Tea Ready ☕

This complete sequence is called a pipeline.

==========

Pipeline in AI / Machine Learning

For example, suppose you want to build a Bakery Sales Prediction AI:

📊 Sales Data
      ↓
🧹 Clean the Data
      ↓
🔄 Prepare / Transform Data
      ↓
🧠 Train the Model
      ↓
📈 Evaluate the Model
      ↓
🚀 Deploy the Model

This sequence is an ML Pipeline.

========

Each step depends on the previous step

For example:

Step 1 → Collect Data
Step 2 → Clean Data
Step 3 → Train Model
Step 4 → Test Model
Step 5 → Deploy Model
Simple definition

Pipeline = A sequence of connected steps that automatically process work from start to finish.

